#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Getting started\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ozone is a web-based moderation interface that allows you to run your own Labeler service, and review and content reports efficiently. This guide will walk you through installing and using Ozone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Installing Ozone\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ozone should be run on a dedicated VPS, from a cloud provider like [OVHcloud](https://us.ovhcloud.com/vps/), [DigitalOcean](https://digitalocean.com/), or [Vultr](https://vultr.com/). 1-2GB of memory and 1-2 CPU cores is sufficient to get started.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "**To install Ozone**, refer to [HOSTING.md](https://github.com/bluesky-social/ozone/blob/main/HOSTING.md) in the [Ozone GitHub repository](https://github.com/bluesky-social/ozone).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Note>\n"
"Before setting up your Ozone service you should create a new account on the network, separate from your main account. This is the account that subscribers to your labeler will interact with: accounts for labelers appear differently in Bluesky than normal accounts.\n"
"</Note>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "After completing the server-side installation, you can access the Ozone web interface by navigating to your server's IP address or domain name in a web browser:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={login} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "From here, you can begin configuring your Labeler service.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Configuring Ozone\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, provide the credentials of the account you created for your labeler service:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={credentials} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "Make sure to provide your full handle, including the `.bsky.social` suffix (or your custom domain if applicable).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, you'll be prompted to update your account registration with the [PLC](https://web.plc.directory/), to mark this account as a moderation service. This will trigger an email verification. Verify that you are using the correct account and domain name, and then provide the verification code:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={plc} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, confirm that you will be using this account as a labeler service. This publishes an [AT Record](https://atproto.at/viewer?uri=did:plc:wwjhjtgw5ksxrzdswtvnsnjs/app.bsky.labeler.service/self) of the type `app.bsky.labeler.service` to your account.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={confirm} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now your Ozone instance is set up and ready to use!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={welcome} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Submitting and managing reports\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, you'll create and action an example moderation report. In Bluesky or another application, sign back in to a regular (non-labeler) account. Then, navigate to the account page for your labeler service.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={labeler} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click the \"Subscribe to Labeler\" button to subscribe your account to the labeler service. This allows your account to submit reports to this labeler, and receive labels from it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, navigate to a post you wish to report, and select \"Report Post\":\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:86
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={report} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because this is just a tutorial, we're going to report a post from Bluesky's own team for being too enthusiastic. This would not normally be a reason to report a post, but it works for our example!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:92
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={reporting} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fill out the reporting interface as desired. Make sure select your labeler as the moderation service to send the report to. Then, submit the report.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, return to the Ozone interface. You should see the new report listed in the *Reports* section:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:100
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={reported} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click on the report to view its details. From here, you can review the reported content and take appropriate moderation actions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={actions} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this case, the most straightforward action is to acknowledge the report without taking further action. Select \"Ackonwledge\" from the drop-down, provide a note, then submit the action. You can use keyboard shortcuts to speed up moderation actions — for example, `S` for Submit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:112
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={acknowledged} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you had wanted to mute the user for subscribers to your labeler, you could have selected \"Mute\" from the action drop-down instead. Refer to [Ozone Concepts](https://github.com/bluesky-social/ozone/blob/main/docs/userguide.md#concepts) for an explanation of each action.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can review the event stream of reports and actions in the *Events* section:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:120
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={eventstream} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "Or, use the *Repositories* section to search reports by user, content, or action:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:126
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={repositories} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:128
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Next steps\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/using-ozone/en.mdx:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "You now have an understanding of the Ozone moderation flow. Ozone also allows you to create additional user accounts with different permissions, to help manage your moderation workload. To aggregate the data from your Ozone instance, see the [#OzoneInsights](https://bsky.app/search?q=%23ozoneinsights) feed for solutions.\n"
msgstr ""

